<%# Jobs (the Mission Control Jobs engine) inside the SkillRx shell, so it looks and works like every
    other admin page: the rail, the page header, design-system tabs, buttons and tables. This file
    overrides the engine's own layout, which loaded Bulma and its own importmap.

    What's overridden: this layout, three partials beside it (_navigation, _flash,
    _application_selection), and the six small partials that hold the engine's buttons
    (app/views/mission_control/jobs/: the action partials, _toolbar, _filters), so buttons carry
    the app's variants. The engine's page templates still render as shipped, with Bulma's class
    names; components/jobs.css gives those the design system's look, scoped to .jobs-engine.
    Overriding every template would fork the gem; on a gem upgrade, diff only these files.
    docs/design/decisions.md, 2026-11-26. %>
<% content_for :title, "#{page_title} · Jobs" %>
<% content_for :shell_content do %>
  <div class="page jobs-engine">
    <% if action_name == "index" %>
      <%# shared/page_header's markup, written out: the partial yields for its actions, and inside a
          layout a bare yield is the page itself, so the list rendered twice. %>
      <header class="page-header"><div class="page-header-titles"><h1>Jobs</h1></div></header>
    <% end %>
    <%= render "layouts/mission_control/jobs/flash" %>
    <%= render "layouts/mission_control/jobs/application_selection" %>
    <%= render "layouts/mission_control/jobs/navigation" %>
    <div class="jobs-body">
      <%= yield %>
    </div>
  </div>
<% end %>
<%= render template: "layouts/application" %>
